# flow_projectnondivergentmultigrid

- Label: Flow Project Non-Divergent Multigrid
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 1 to 4
- Parameters: 6 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/flow_projectnondivergentmultigrid.html
- Summary (EN): This node removes divergent components from a 2D vector field, producing a valid velocity field for incompressible flow. It is used inside a Flow block, and it makes distortion swirl around sources and sinks rather than pulling flow into them.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Flow Project Non-Divergent Multigrid retire les composantes divergentes d'un champ de vecteurs 2D pour obtenir un écoulement incompressible valide.

- Inputs meaning: ["v: initial velocity field to correct", "goaldiv (optional): goal divergence field; positive areas create sources and negative areas create sinks", "collision (optional): mask where 1 marks the collider location", "collisionv (optional): velocity field for the collider; if omitted, the collider is treated as stationary"]

- Key parameters: ["Collision Iterations: passes used to avoid the collider; more passes give better avoidance but longer execution times", "Multigrid Iterations: multigrid passes used to match the goal divergence; more passes give closer matching but longer execution times", "X Borders and Y Borders: edge behavior per axis; Open lets flow leave without resistance, Closed acts as a solid wall, Periodic wraps flow to the opposite side"]

- Caveats: ["Flow requires DOP-level permissions; it is not available in Houdini Core, only in Houdini FX, Apprentice, Indie and Education", "Collision handling is soft; if the output does not match the collider well enough, the node may need to be iterated for better convergence"]

